R_INIT="The Academic health data transparency work that was a subset of our larger academic health work so I'll I'll set the scene a little bit. Every school on our network had grade books, they had tons of data, All of that data was in kind of these large CSV files and Excel files. and While it was accessible or while it was there, people couldn't really use it."
R_INIT2="Using Cloud Code to build A Python script that parsed out these huge data sets and with the push of a button created individualized teacher reports Telling them, you know, here are the students of concern, the assignments of concern. Here's where you don't have enough of a certain type of assessment. Here's where, you know, you're Your grades seem to be skewing. So we got people weekly high quality personalized data that we were able to compare to a standard. We did the same thing for students."
R_INIT3="I designed this for one particular school, rolled it out at that school, and then we took it across the country. And so, We built these reports through the AI. Then we created a regular kind of meeting cadence We created a team at the school I was looking into these things and was leading the work on the ground."
R_INIT4="And what we ended up seeing was instead of people waiting till The end of the quarter to finish the grading or to tell students kind of where they stood and what needed to happen, they were able to do that. weekly and just the fact that the data went from present but obscured to right in front of them, drove a tremendous amount of positive change because, again, they could look at it and they could see This is where I'm falling short. This is where this student is struggling."
R_INIT5="We then took that across the country and we were able to see the biggest jump in GPA year over year in that, in kind of the last year. In our last quarter that I was there, of course there's a million things that go into creating huge GPA jumps, so I don't mean to, I'm not trying to take all the credit, but it's been cited as one of the primary Drivers that really got the right folks Focus on the right conversation and the right actions."
